<h4>Discussions</h4>
<p>Discussions are graded on completion: one original post of at least 250 words, plus replies to at least two classmates. Posts that fail to meet the basic requirements will not count toward completion. See Section 3 below for full discussion expectations.</p>
<h4>Quizzes</h4>
<p>Quizzes are multiple choice and graded automatically. Each quiz covers the reading for that unit. You have 60 minutes and one attempt per quiz. See Section 2 for full quiz and exam instructions.</p>
<h4>Term Paper</h4>
<p>The term paper is a minimum of three pages in MLA format. Paper topics are provided in Unit 2; a Paper Preparation Exercise in Unit 2 walks you through the process before your final submission. See the Paper Preparation Exercise Instructions for the full grading criteria.</p>
<h4>Final Exam</h4>
<p>The final exam is a comprehensive essay exam covering all six units. It is the last item in the course and becomes available after you complete Unit 6.</p>
<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span><div class="callout__content">
<p>Where to find your assignments</p>
<p>All assignments appear in the Modules page, organized by unit. You can also see them on the Assignments page. Grades are posted in the Grades section as they are entered.</p>
</div></div>
