<h3>What each quiz covers</h3>
<p>There are six unit quizzes and one final exam. Each quiz covers the reading assigned for that unit:</p>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 1:</strong> Plato, <em>Euthyphro</em>, <em>Apology</em>, and <em>Crito</em></div>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 2:</strong> Descartes, <em>Meditations on First Philosophy</em></div>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 3:</strong> Hume, <em>Enquiry Concerning Human Understanding</em> (Sections 1–5)</div>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 4:</strong> Hegel, <em>Introduction to the Philosophy of History</em> (pp. 14–96)</div>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 5:</strong> Marx, <em>Communist Manifesto</em></div>
<div>— <strong>Quiz 6:</strong> Sartre, <em>Existentialism Is a Humanism</em></div>
<div>— <strong>Final Exam:</strong> comprehensive essay test covering all six units</div>
<h4>Taking a quiz</h4>
<p>Quizzes are taken online through Canvas. You can find them at the end of each unit module, or through the Quizzes link in the course navigation.</p>
<div>— You have <strong>60 minutes</strong> per quiz and <strong>one attempt only</strong></div>
<div>— Each quiz is available from the start of the course until its due date</div>
<div>— No late submissions are accepted</div>
<div>— Grades are posted automatically in the Grades section</div>
<div class="callout callout--connection"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">➡️</span><div class="callout__content">
<p>Don’t wait until the last minute</p>
<p>Technical problems just before a deadline do not guarantee an extension. Give yourself a buffer of at least a day before the due date. If a genuine emergency prevents you from taking a quiz, contact your instructor through the Canvas Inbox as soon as possible — before the deadline if at all possible.</p>
</div></div>
<h4>Make-up policy</h4>
<p>A missed quiz receives a zero unless you request a make-up in writing through the Canvas Inbox before or immediately after the deadline. Make-ups are granted only for documented illness, legal matters, or other serious extenuating circumstances — not for needing more study time.</p>
<p>If you need a make-up, contact your instructor no later than the next weekday after the missed deadline and be prepared to provide documentation.</p>
<h4>Practice first</h4>
<p>Before you take your first quiz, practice the submission process using the Syllabus Quiz in this module. It’s open book, has a required score of 100%, and must be completed before the rest of the course unlocks. For help with the quiz interface, see <a href="https://community.instructure.com/en/kb/articles/662767-what-are-quizzes" target="_blank">How do I take a quiz?</a> in the Canvas Student Guide.</p>
</div></div><div class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="tabs-0-panel-2" aria-labelledby="tabs-0-tab-2" hidden=""><div>
<h3>What discussions are for</h3>
<p>Philosophy is fundamentally a dialogic practice — it happens between people, through argument and response. The discussion boards in this course are the closest equivalent we have to the kind of exchange that would happen in a classroom. They are not a formality; they are part of how the thinking gets done.</p>
<p>You will participate in one discussion per unit. You can find them in the Modules page or through the Discussions link in the course navigation.</p>
<h4>Your initial post</h4>
<p>Each post should be at least 250 words (one to two well-developed paragraphs). Your post should address the discussion question directly, exhibit careful reasoning, and support your position with evidence or argument — not just assert it. Use correct spelling, punctuation, and grammar.</p>
<h4>Replies to classmates</h4>
<p>Reply to at least two other students for each discussion. Replies should add something substantive — a new argument, a question that pushes the thinking further, or a respectful disagreement. Replies that simply agree or restate what was said do not meet the requirement.</p>
<p>Disagreement is welcome. Philosophy thrives on it. What matters is that you disagree with ideas, not people, and that you remain courteous and open to having your own position challenged.</p>
